// Undertaking Tension Events (D20), p.80-81.
(
    name: "Undertaking Tension Event",
    die: D20,
    entries: [
        (1, 1, (title: "Flesh Burrower Ambush", text: "The ground beneath your feet suddenly softens and writhes. Tendrils of sinew erupt from the soil, attempting to drag you down while partially formed mouths snap at your ankles. The very earth is trying to eat you.")),
        (2, 2, (title: "The Choir's Patrol", text: "A procession of Penitents appears on the road ahead. They are not marching, but performing a slow, hypnotic ritual of conversion on a captive. They will perceive you as either new congregants to be forcibly converted or blasphemous dissonance to be silenced.")),
        (3, 3, (title: "The Witch Hunters", text: "A group of grim, torch-wielding zealots, unaffiliated with the Choir, corners the party. They are \"Purifiers\" who believe any survivor is inherently tainted (except themselves, of course). They demand a confession of your sins and will \"cleanse\" you by fire if your answers displease them.")),
        (4, 4, (title: "Crossfire", text: "You blunder into a fresh battlefield. A Choir patrol and a pack of Flesh-spawn are locked in a brutal, ongoing struggle. Both sides will treat you as an immediate threat, forcing you to navigate a chaotic three-way battle.")),
        (5, 5, (title: "Ambush!", text: "You find something that could prove an advantage, but in reality is nothing but a lure. As soon as you approach, camouflaged cultists of the Choir close in for the kill.")),
        (6, 6, (title: "The Cannibals", text: "A ragged band of starving survivors blocks your path. Their eyes are wild with hunger, their weapons are crude but deadly. They don't want your supplies; they want you. This is not for ritual, only for food.")),
        (7, 7, (title: "The Hunt", text: "A pack of Flesh Apostates, more cunning than mindless beasts, has been stalking you. They use the terrain to their advantage, setting crude traps and attempting to separate the party before striking from the shadows of a fleshy corruption they have seeded.")),
        (8, 8, (title: "The Watcher in the Sky", text: "A high-ranking Choir entity—a winged Seraph of sculpted mouths and dissonant chords—hovers in the sky above. Its gaze is a weapon, potentially causing Anguish and change. While you are distracted, its earth-bound minions attack.")),
        (9, 9, (title: "Echoes of Battle", text: "You enter a place of great slaughter. The spectral echoes of a past battle play out around you. The ghostly combatants—knights, Penitents, Apostates—can pass through you, but their weapons and abilities inflict real, spiritual wounds.")),
        (10, 10, (title: "The Intervention", text: "Just as you are about to achieve your goal, a rival party or individual from your past appears. They have no intention of letting you succeed and will do anything to stop you and claim the prize for themselves.")),
        (11, 11, (title: "The Ground Gives Away", text: "The earth cracks open, not from a Flesh-quake, but into a deep chasm. The fall is treacherous, and at the bottom is the nesting ground of some subterranean horror awoken by the tremor. The only way out is up, or through.")),
        (12, 12, (title: "Reanimated Blasphemy", text: "A Choir \"Artisan\" has been at work here. With the help of prayer, it has animated the bodies from a graveyard into a grotesque mockery of life. These puppets attack with the zealous fury of the Choir's song.")),
        (13, 13, (title: "No Longer Neutral", text: "The neutral guardian of a location you need to access has deemed you a threat. Whether a pagan spirit worker, a group of scavengers, or just a community of survivors, they will now use the full extent of their power to drive you out or destroy you.")),
        (14, 14, (title: "The Silent Hunter", text: "The air grows still and all sound dies, including your own voices. A creature of the Flesh that seems to spread absolute silence around itself is near.")),
        (15, 15, (title: "The Flesh Host", text: "A massive creature, seemingly a beast of the Flesh, is slain. Its body then explodes, releasing a swarm of smaller, faster horrors that were gestating inside. You are suddenly at the center of a writhing horde.")),
        (16, 16, (title: "The Mob", text: "A charismatic Unbroken has convinced a mob of desperate refugees that you are the cause of their suffering, that you hoard resources or draw the monsters. Whipped into a frenzy, they descend upon you with farm tools and torches.")),
        (17, 17, (title: "The Land Apostate", text: "A Flesh Apostate turns the environment itself into a weapon against you. Trees lash like whips, stones are spat by the fleshy soil against you, and the air becomes thick with miasma. You must fight both the Apostate and the land it commands.")),
        (18, 18, (title: "The Price of Your Past", text: "An enemy from a character's backstory (a wronged man, a vengeful spirit, a former comrade) appears, now empowered by the Choir or the Flesh. They have been given the strength to exact their revenge and have been waiting for this moment.")),
        (19, 19, (title: "Betrayal", text: "A supposed ally reveals their true nature. They lead you directly into a well-planned ambush, disabling your strengths and exploiting your weaknesses.")),
        (20, 20, (title: "The Champion", text: "You have gone too far. You have threatened something the Choir or the Flesh cannot afford to lose. In response, they send a Champion—a uniquely powerful Penitent, a prime specimen of the Flesh, or a similarly named entity of terrifying repute. This is not a random encounter; this is an execution.")),
    ],
)
